\ A wrong twin of s2-rfl-id.lf (tests/front/check_s2.py, s2-wrong.lean's
\ w_rfl_id): eq_refl fails on a = b, and applyRfl's whnfR keeps id, a
\ relation of two arguments whose sides Prop and a = b differ, so rfl
\ fails with Lean's message (error 97). The goal line differs: LeanForth's
\ printer shows @id Prop (a = b) where Lean's hides the implicit argument
\ (plan 8.6); the comparison takes the lines before it.
\ Lean: theorem w_rfl_id (a b : Nat) : id (a = b) := by rfl
theorem w_rfl_id
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = id
:= by
  by-rfl
end w_rfl_id
